Source: stellarbox
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Stellarbox CMake fork <nobody@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cmake, pkg-config, gcc, libx11-dev, libxcb1-dev, libxext-dev, libxft-dev, libxrandr-dev, libxrender-dev, libxshape-dev, libglib2.0-dev, libxml2-dev, libcairo2-dev, libpango1.0-dev, librsvg2-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: stellarbox
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, python3, picom, polybar | tint2, rofi | dmenu, feh | nitrogen, dunst, x11-xserver-utils, dbus-x11, mate-polkit | polkit-gnome | lxqt-policykit | xfce-polkit, stellarbox-obconf (>= 0.16.6)
Provides: x-window-manager, x-session-manager
Description: A minimalistic, highly configurable X11 window manager
 Stellarbox (formerly Openbox) is a lightweight, highly configurable X11
 window manager with extensive standards support (EWMH/ICCCM), built from
 the CMake-customized fork with vector (Cairo) rendering, rounded corners,
 HiDPI support and _NET_WM_OPAQUE_REGION.